// Sigil-Logic/clafer#18: a reference target the chocosolver DSL cannot
// express -- here a set expression mixing a clafer and an integer --
// makes the Choco backend decline the whole model through its
// unsupported-feature path ("Choco output unavailable because the
// model contains: a reference target the Choco backend cannot express
// (c0_mixed: ...)", exit 0, no .js) instead of emitting a silently
// under-constrained model.  Alloy accepts the union, so the .als,
// .html, and .dot outputs are still generated and baselined; the .js
// is absent from both the generated tree and the .reg corpus, as for
// every other declined model.

abstract Person

Alice : Person

mixed -> Person ++ 1
